{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Of the turtledoves or of the young of pigeons.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Scripture chose the grown ones among turtledoves because of devotion, for the female among them, when she loses her mate, will never cling to another; and so Israel, who cleave to the Holy One, blessed be He, will never exchange Him for another. Therefore He disqualified the small ones before they are fit for mating. And among pigeons He disqualified the grown ones because they are jealous toward all others, which leads to separation; therefore He chose the small ones before they are fit for mating. And the reason the Torah did not permit roosters for the altar is that they are creatures of lust." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the turtledoves — their root is water, and therefore the grown ones were permitted, to allude that Ḥesed is a great necessity for the world in all things; and the pigeons — their root is fire, as it is written of the pigeon (Psalms 68:14): ״ואברותיה בירקרק חרוץ״, for gold is the greenish hue of fire, and the redoubling in ירקרק is for the intensity of judgment, and therefore the grown ones were disqualified and the small ones were permitted, for a small amount of it suffices."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:31.118839854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}